# 3. IMPORTANT PRODUCT DESIGN PRINCIPLE

**THE USER INTERFACE MUST SPEAK THE LANGUAGE OF THE USER, NOT THE LANGUAGE OF THE IMPLEMENTATION.**

Reviewers should see:

- Hồ sơ sinh viên.
- Sơ tuyển.
- Danh sách đề nghị xét chọn.
- Văn bản đề nghị.
- Gửi danh sách lên Thành phố.
- Xét duyệt.
- Thẩm định.
- Yêu cầu bổ sung.
- Kết quả xét chọn.

They should not be forced to understand:

- Workflow state.
- Batch lifecycle.
- Read-only lock.
- Internal status transitions.
- Canonical snapshot.
- Technical validation.
- Resource scope.
- AI confidence.
- Processing engine.
- Review orchestration.

These technical concepts may still exist internally.

They do not belong in normal user-facing copy unless essential to a real administrative task.

